{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>If the left, and I will go right.</b> That is, if you go left, and I will go right — I will go south, for there his direction was set to go, as it is written above, 'הלוך ונסוע הנגבה' — 'going on and journeying toward the Negev.' And 'the right' means: if you wish to go south, 'ואשמאילה' — that is, I will move myself left. Thus Rashi interpreted." "And one may wonder how he could say 'ואשמאילה' meaning 'I will move myself left' when Abraham's intention was to go south. But the explanation of <b>ואשמאילה</b> is: 'I will move you left' — that is, you will perforce have to go north. And so I have heard that the translation of Onkelos in precise manuscripts reads: 'אם את לצפונא ואנא לדרומא ואם את לדרומא ואצפנך' — 'if you go north I will go south, and if you go south I will go north' — that is, perforce, for I will not give you permission to remain in the south because of the weight of the cattle that I have.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:12:11.771283589Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}